{% extends 'home/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}CenterTime - Frequently Asked Questions{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <!-- FAQ Section -->
    <section class="d-flex flex-column gap-12 mt-6 mb-12 reveal-right">
        <div class="text-center">
            <h1 class="fs-3xl">Frequently Asked <span class="text-gradient">Questions</span></h1>
            <p class="fs-lg text-secondary mt-2 ml-auto mr-auto max-w-700">
                Common questions regarding multi-tenant time clocks and manager policy options.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-6 m-0 w-100 max-w-800 ml-auto mr-auto">
            <!-- Compliance Checklist Panel -->
            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-xl mb-4 fw-700 text-gradient d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="material-icons text-primary">assignment_turned_in</span>
                    Checklist
                </h3>
                <div class="compliance-table-wrapper">
                    <table class="compliance-table">
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="req-col">Digital System Required</td>
                                <td>
                                    <span class="material-icons text-success fs-md align-middle" style="margin-right: 8px;">check_circle</span> CenterTime provides a fully digital multi-tenant kiosk platform. Attendance check-ins are logged electronically, replacing manual clipboards, paper rosters, and standalone spreadsheet trackers.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="req-col">Unique Student Identification</td>
                                <td>
                                    <span class="material-icons text-success fs-md align-middle" style="margin-right: 8px;">check_circle</span> Each student accounts roster record is assigned a unique system ID, custom name, secure individual PIN code, and QR Code badge identifier to ensure clear, non-overlapping identities.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="req-col">Actual Arrival and Departure</td>
                                <td>
                                    <span class="material-icons text-success fs-md align-middle" style="margin-right: 8px;">check_circle</span> Check-in and check-out logs record exact, real-time timestamps upon student check-in entry rather than post-hoc manual entry, ensuring high data accuracy and audit compliance.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="req-col">Current Student Awareness</td>
                                <td>
                                    <span class="material-icons text-success fs-md align-middle" style="margin-right: 8px;">check_circle</span> CenterTime's real-time manager dashboard exposes an active session roster view, showing exactly which students are currently checked in at the facility at any given second.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="req-col">Backup or Data Preservation Approach</td>
                                <td>
                                    <span class="material-icons text-success fs-md align-middle" style="margin-right: 8px;">check_circle</span> Our system database is backed up regularly. Additionally, managers can export timesheets and user roster data locally in CSV and Excel formats at any point for offline archiving.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="req-col">Appropriate Handling of Student Information / Personally Identifiable Information (PII)</td>
                                <td>
                                    <span class="material-icons text-success fs-md align-middle" style="margin-right: 8px;">check_circle</span> CenterTime hashes check-in PIN credentials securely, restricts data access via authorization tokens, uses math captcha filters to block bots, masks student last names on public-facing check-in pages for added security, and keeps student data isolated inside dedicated organization silos.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="req-col">Reviewable and Retained Records</td>
                                <td>
                                    <span class="material-icons text-success fs-md align-middle" style="margin-right: 8px;">check_circle</span> Student attendance records are retained securely and can be reviewed directly in the manager dashboard. Once your plan's history data retention window (e.g. 61, 184, or 366 days) expires, all past attendance records are permanently purged from our database systems and cannot be recovered by any means.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-lg mb-2 fw-700">How fast can we set up CenterTime for our organization?</h3>
                <p class="fs-md text-secondary lh-base m-0">
                    You can launch in under 2 minutes. Simply sign up for your organization, choose a URL slug, and start logging check-ins via our web kiosk or importing your roster CSV.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-lg mb-2 fw-700">How do subscription licensing limits affect my organization?</h3>
                <p class="fs-md text-secondary lh-base m-0">
                    Licensing plans restrict student limits, history retention windows, and kiosk features. Basic plans support open lists, whereas Silver, Gold, and Platinum tiers unlock the secure PIN keypad. Contactless QR code scan modes and PDF badge generation are restricted to Gold and Platinum plans.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-lg mb-2 fw-700">What check-in and checkout kiosk modes are available?</h3>
                <p class="fs-md text-secondary lh-base m-0">
                    We support three distinct checkout/check-in methods:
                    <br>1. <strong>Click List - Check in</strong>: Tap on names from an open roster dropdown.
                    <br>2. <strong>Secure PIN - Check in</strong>: Enter a unique 4-digit PIN to clock in.
                    <br>3. <strong>QR Code scan - Check in</strong>: Scan scannable badges via webcam/camera scanner for hands-free instant logging.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-lg mb-2 fw-700">How does the CSV spreadsheet roster import work?</h3>
                <p class="fs-md text-secondary lh-base m-0">
                    The spreadsheet importer maps columns dynamically to student profiles. It checks for duplicates using fuzzy matching rules, warns you if you are exceeding your license student quotas, and lets you verify name matches before finalizing the onboarding.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-lg mb-2 fw-700">How do custom overrides work?</h3>
                <p class="fs-md text-secondary lh-base m-0">
                    If a tenant requires more capacity than their standard plan permits (e.g. extra student seats or categories limits), the platform super-administrator can add individual overrides from the Organizations controller, storing only overridden parameters at the database level.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-lg mb-2 fw-700">What happens when a subscription payment fails?</h3>
                <p class="fs-md text-secondary lh-base m-0">
                    If a renewal payment fails via Stripe, the subscription changes to overdue, locking premium manager actions and blocking kiosk access screens until resolved.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-lg mb-2 fw-700">Can students check in outside schedule hours?</h3>
                <p class="fs-md text-secondary lh-base m-0">
                    Managers can configure absolute time windows. If a student clocks in outside this period, their check-in transaction completes successfully but is flagged immediately in audit records and dashboard reports.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-lg mb-2 fw-700">How are active sessions left open prevented from staying active indefinitely?</h3>
                <p class="fs-md text-secondary lh-base m-0">
                    The platform's background auto-termination sweeper automatically ends open clock-in sessions that exceed the maximum allowed shift duration limit.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-lg mb-2 fw-700">What security measures protect the kiosk from unauthorized PIN guessing?</h3>
                <p class="fs-md text-secondary lh-base m-0">
                    If a student enters an incorrect PIN 3 times in a row, the platform triggers an anti-brute force lockout. The student account is immediately disabled until cleared by a manager.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="glass-panel p-6">
                <h3 class="fs-lg mb-2 fw-700">Does CenterTime guarantee the physical presence of a student on our premises?</h3>
                <p class="fs-md text-secondary lh-base m-0">
                    No. Our systems are only as reliable as their administrative usage. It is the sole responsibility of the center's instructors and managers to perform timely checks and supervise check-ins/checkouts. CenterTime purely records attendance logging events based on system inputs and access credentials; it does not track physical location or guarantee the actual presence or absence of any student on the premises.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
